mulation where the background reads are uniformly distributed (low coverage) and the \"exome\" targets have ~30x coverage. The depth ≥ 20 regions ≈ true targets (exons). Total target size 474 kb — hmm, that's too small for the whole chr9 exome.\n\nWhatever the design, the analysis strategy is the same: call variants at positions with sufficient depth (DP ≥ 15–20), look for heterozygous/mosaic ALT support, filter by quality, then annotate for nonsense mutations within protein-coding genes.\n\nAlright, let me run bcftools mpileup/call on the nodup BAM with reasonable minimums, and also do a sensitive mosaic-oriented scan."}}
