stop_gained/stop_lost, etc. Position within the CDS: need to handle strand and CDS phase (compute cumulative CDS length from the start codon; frame = (cumulative offset) mod 3).\n  - A stop_gained is nonsense. Must be premature (i.e., not replacing the natural stop codon — that would be stop_lost... actually, if the variant is within the last codon of the stop, the alt creates a stop at the natural stop position → not nonsense. If the ref codon is a stop and the alt is an amino acid → stop_lost).\n- Combine with AF from the allsites scan.\n\nGene-level LoF intolerance: fetch gnomAD constraint (LOEUF, pLI) via the network for the identified genes.\n\nLet's first analyze the called variants: parse work/calls.vcf and compute the AF distribution. Let's write a quick Python script in WSL (python3 3.12)."}}
