{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"reasoning","text":"Format of allsites.tsv: chrom, pos, ref, alt (`<*>` at invariant sites), DP (empty in these rows? Wait, column 5 is empty in these rows). Hmm — DP is empty at invariant sites, because FORMAT/DP is only emitted at variant sites? Actually, bcftools mpileup outputs FORMAT fields per sample. At invariant sites, the sample field may just be \"0/0\" with no DP. The AD column displays \"0,0\". So DP is empty at invariant sites. No problem — invariant sites aren't interesting.\n\nWait, but I need to double-check the awk parsing inside step4: for the DP column I was looking for fields matching /^DP:/ starting from field 9. If the FORMAT at variant sites is GT:AD:DP, then $9=\"0/1:5,10:15\" — the whole field contains DP as the 3rd colon-separated element, not as an independent field. My awk was splitting $j (each field from 9 onward) by \":\" and taking f[2] — that's wrong: I split the whole FORMAT+sample field… Actually, looking at it: for j=9, `$j ~ /^DP:/` is never true, because $9 = \"GT:AD:DP\" (the FORMAT string). In other words, the dp column in allsites.tsv is always empty! Let me verify with a variant row."}}
