{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"reasoning","text":"Confirmed — the DP column is empty (parsing bug). But AD is there: e.g. \"0,2,0\" = ref,alt,<*>. There are 39,975 rows that have an actual ALT allele (including low-count ones; the count here is without duplicates but with -q 30 -Q 20).\n\nI don't need DP from this file — total = sum of AD. Let me redo the mosaic scan properly in Python: parse allsites.tsv, compute AF for each ALT (excluding <*>), and keep positions where alt_count>=3 and AF within the range [0.03, 0.97] and total>=10. Then annotate.\n\nAlso, for strand balance info, I should re-extract ADF/ADR at candidate positions — can handle that later with targeted samtools mpileup or bcftools query at candidate positions.\n\nOK, so let me write a comprehensive analysis script. Write it as work/analyze.py (this will evolve into the final output/analysis.py). Components:\n\n1. FASTA loading: parse work/GRCh38_chr9.fa → dict of sequences (uppercase).\n2. GTF loading: protein-coding transcripts with CDS.\n3. Variant input:\n   a. Called variants from work/calls.vcf (SNVs only, with AD).\n   b. Mosaic scan from work/allsites.tsv.\n4. Annotation function: annotate(pos, ref, alt) → list of (gene_name, gene_id, transcript_id, consequence, cds_pos, aa_change).\n5. Filter + rank; output table of stop_gained candidates.\n6. LoF intolerance check via gene symbol (fetch externally later).\n\nReading frame details: use GTF's frame column (0,1,2 = number of bases to skip at feature start for CDS entries) or compute from CDS order. Computing from order is more robust: sort CDS segments in transcription order; concatenate segment sequences; verify length is a multiple of 3 and that translation starts with M and ends with *. GENCODE CDS should be accurate. To be safe, verify: CDS total length % 3 == 0; first codon is ATG; last codon is a stop. If a transcript fails, skip it (or mark it as abnormal).\n\nRegarding phase: use GTF's phase column (if available) to double-check my own computed frame at each CDS start. Actually the simplest is: concatenate CDS in transcription order → full CDS sequence; then for a variant at CDS offset o (0-based from CDS start), codon = cds[o - o%3 : o - o%3 + 3].\n\nStrand handling: for minus strand, CDS segments are sorted by descending coordinate; each segment's sequence is reverse-complemented; the variant offset within a segment = seg_end - p (since transcription proceeds from higher to lower coordinates).\n\nOK let me write the script.\n\nAlso: handle the case where a variant is within CDS but the position within the codon is... covered.\n\nConsequence categories to assign (simplified, SNV only):\n- intergenic / intronic / UTR (5'UTR, 3'UTR) — based on transcript features (exon vs CDS vs UTR). UTR can be inferred: exon regions not in CDS (before CDS start → 5'UTR, after → 3'UTR).\n- splice_donor/acceptor: within intron 1..2 bases of exon boundary.\n- stop_gained, stop_lost, missense, synonymous, start_lost (first codon), incomplete_terminal_codon (if offset lands in last incomplete codon — skip).\n\nRank candidates for the task: stop_gained + mosaic AF + DP/AD quality + strand balance.\n\nOK let me write the code. Write it in the workspace so it can be reused, then run it under WSL python3.\n\nOne more thing: for strand balance I need ADF/ADR. When I regenerate the candidate list, run bcftools mpileup with -a ADF,ADR at candidate positions via a region file. Do that after candidate selection.\n\nAlso, I realized I should re-check duplicate handling: I used nodup (duplicates excluded). The AF of the mosaic variant in deduped reads is the correct estimate.\n\nAdditionally, I want to check that the mosaic candidate is not in a low-complexity/repeat region — alignment artifacts. bwa's MAPQ60 + baseQ20 helps. Check for nearby homopolymers in the reference sequence around the candidate.\n\nOK, writing analyze.py.\n"}}
