{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_123","type":"reasoning","text":"Currently, 2500 out of 2998 protein-coding transcripts have valid CDS.\n\nNext, the main discovery script:\n1. Load FASTA + GTF and build the index.\n2. Scan allsites.tsv to identify mosaic candidates: alt_count ≥ 3, total ≥ 10, AF within [0.03, 0.97]. Also annotate the called variants from calls.vcf.\n3. Annotate candidates with stop_gained.\n4. For stop_gained candidates: fetch strand bias data via targeted mpileup (bcftools mpileup with ADF/ADR over the region) — or better yet, re-run mpileup over the entire genome with ADF/ADR and capture only candidate positions. Since candidates are few, use bcftools mpileup -r chr9:pos-pos.\n\nAlright, let's write discover.py.\n"}}
