il -1 line shows \"A\" — hmm, is the faidx output header line \"chr9:127661095-127661155\" followed by the sequence? Only \"A\" is displayed — strange. Actually the sequence might be on multiple lines, and tail -1 grabbed the last line \"A\"? 61bp in a 60-char-wide format: line 1 = 60 chars, line 2 = 1 char \"A\". So tail -1 only shows \"A\". Let me output the entire region. Also, no nearby variants in calls.vcf within ±50bp of the STXBP1 site (awk found nothing — wait, the output of awk | cut shows nothing under the header; grep -v '#' may have found nothing. Actually the awk output should appear after the header, but nothing was output → no nearby variants. Good — the site is isolated.\n\nNow, base quality and mapping quality of the 6 ALT-supporting reads, plus positions within reads and read names — let me investigate more carefully. Also check whether the ALT reads have soft clips nearby or are at read ends. Use samtools mpileup -Q 20 (default) and compare counts: with -Q 0 we got 47; if some bases have baseQ < 20, the -Q 20 depth will drop.\n\nAdditionally, do formal variant calling at this site with bcftools using a low AF threshold, and get QUAL etc. Or use `bcftools mpileup` + `bcftools call -m` with the site list.\n\nLet me gather:\n1. Full reference context (60bp on both sides).\n2. Counts at baseQ>=20 and baseQ>=30.\n3. Per-base baseQ and mapq of ALT-supporting reads: can be extracted from BAM with samtools view -L region + python CIGAR parsing, or use `samtools mpileup -B -Q 0 --output-extra QNAME,MAPQ`... htslib's mpileup has an -s/--output-extra option that outputs QNAME etc. Use `samtools mpileup -s -O` (per-sample) → VCF-style output? Actually `-s` outputs per-sample counts. More simply: use `samtools view` and parse with a small python script using CIGAR — or even more simply, `samtools mpileup --output QNAME` is unavailable. Let me use python + the BAM: hmm, no pysam.\n\nAlternative: `samtools view work/aln.nodup.bam chr9:127661125-127661125` retur