{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_148","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting — STXBP1 is on the plus strand in this annotation! Wait, but in the discover.py output the codon was GAA>TAA with aa=E103*. On the plus strand, the reference base at 127661125 is G, and the variant is G>T. Codon GAA (Glu) → TAA (stop). This is consistent with the plus strand: codon GAA at the genomic position.\n\nWait, I previously thought STXBP1 was on the minus strand, but the GTF says it's on the plus strand. Let me re-verify: STXBP1 in GRCh38 is at chr9:127,611,760-127,696,027... actually, according to UCSC, STXBP1 is at chr9:127,612,270-127,692,707 on the minus strand? Hmm. In GENCODE, STXBP1 is on the forward strand? Let me check the GTF directly: the transcript strand column showed '+'. And the codon GAA at position 127661125: reference G (matches the reference base G from mpileup), and the codon read forward is GAA. Since the reference base is G and G>T produces TAA (stop), the codon must be 5'-GAA-3' on the plus strand. Consistent.\n\nHmm wait, but UCSC shows STXBP1 on the minus strand... actually, let me verify: STXBP1 (syntaxin binding protein 1) is at GRCh38 chr9:127,611,760-127,696,027, and according to NCBI the gene is on the plus strand? NCBI Gene: STXBP1 is at GRCh38 chr9:127,611,760-127,696,027, on the forward strand? I recall STXBP1 being transcribed in the direction from centromere to telomere... The GTF here explicitly says '+'. I'll trust the provided GTF.\n\nCanonical transcript: ENST00000373299.5 (STXBP1-201) with the Ensembl_canonical tag. According to my annotation output: ENST00000373299.5 → E117* (codon 117), ENST00000626333.2 → E103*. In the discover.py output: ENST00000373299.5 aa=E117*. Therefore, for the canonical transcript the consequence is p.Glu117Ter (E117*).\n\nSo for reporting purposes: canonical transcript ENST00000373299.5 (STXBP1-201), codon 117, GAA>TAA, p.Glu117*.\n\nExon: exon 6 (chr9:127661102-127661205) of the canonical transcript (19