d in GENCODE v47.\n- LoF intolerance: gnomAD v4: pLI ≈ 1.0 (0.999999999999999), o/e LoF = 0.0382, 95% CI [0.0174, 0.0987], lof_z = 7.23, expected LoF 78.5 vs observed 3. Classification: highly LoF-intolerant (pLI≥0.9, o/e upper CI ≤0.35). STXBP1 is associated with developmental and epileptic encephalopathy (DEE) due to haploinsufficiency; LOF is the established disease mechanism.\n- Rejected candidates:\n  - GRIN3A chr9:101,670,953 C>T p.G487* AF 0.55 → germline heterozygous (p=0.5 is not rejected), GRIN3A o/e LoF 0.51, pLI 5e-6 (tolerant).\n  - ALAD chr9:113,391,620 A>G p.Y56* AF 0.619 → germline heterozygous-like, ALAD tolerant (o/e 0.45, pLI 0.047).\n  - COL27A1 chr9:114,196,007 C>T p.R707* AF 0.182 (4/23): only 4 ALT reads, all on the reverse strand (strand-biased artifact), gene is LoF-tolerant.\n  - C5 chr9:121,017,727 G>A p.Y544* AF 0.475 → germline heterozygous, C5 is tolerant.\n- Tools and versions: bwa 0.7.17-r1188, samtools 1.19.2 (htslib 1.19), bcftools 1.19, Python 3.12.3; samtools/bcftools/bwa binaries: Ubuntu 24.04 packages run via WSL.\n- Coordinate system: GRCh38, 1-based; sequence name chr9.\n- Date of analysis: 2026-08-28.\n- Deliverables and reproduction steps: python3 output/analysis.py --workspace . (requires bwa/samtools/bcftools on PATH or TOOL_DIR).\n\nLet me check the re-run results before writing the report."}}
